        "original_id": "a9a98666-7d26-5785-b09b-4f2ff0dd7df1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Manru, A Hut Behind the Village\n- People: Ignacy Jan Paderewski, Alfred Nossig, Henry Edward Krehbiel, Józef Ignacy Kraszewski\n- Topics: opera, libretto, Polish independence\n\nFacts:\n- In 1843, Józef Ignacy Kraszewski published the novel \"A Hut Behind the Village.\"\n- Ignacy Jan Paderewski was born on 18 November 1860 and died on 29 June 1941.\n- Ignacy Jan Paderewski was a Polish pianist, composer, politician, and spokesman for Polish independence.\n- Manru is an opera in three acts with music composed by Ignacy Jan Paderewski.\n- Manru uses a libretto by Alfred Nossig.\n- Henry Edward Krehbiel made the English translation of the libretto for Manru.\n- Manru was based on Józef Ignacy Kraszewski's 1843 novel \"A Hut Behind the Village.\"",
